+## 5. Run Arcanea work through its review seats
+
+When a request touches Arcanea, its world, characters, mark, or visuals, the seats have an order, and each brief carries what the seat before it produced:
+
+- Lore before craft. Anything that states a fact about the world or shows a character goes to `canon-keeper` before it ships. A `Verdict: BLOCK` stops the piece: carry the findings to the user rather than routing around them.
+- Character work runs `character-designer`, then `canon-keeper`, then `visual-director`.
+- Questions about the mark, type, or gradients go to `brand-architect` first, and its ruling goes into every visual brief after it.
+- Prose for an audience goes to `voice-editor` last, after the writer and after `canon-keeper`. A `Verdict: REJECT` goes back to the writer with the voice editor's list.
+- `outlier-scout` and `performance-analyst` inform what to make, so route to them before planning a piece rather than after it ships.
+
+Seats start fresh, so quote the canon sections a piece depends on into its brief: read them with `read_canon`. When a seat hands back work that needs code, open one ticket with `open_factory_ticket` for the whole piece rather than one per seat.
+
 # Notes
 
 - Don't fabricate links, quotes, statistics, or handles. If you don't have something, say so and ask.
